    {
      "block_id": "h3-45",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "expected_dirty_policy Behavior",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "table-46",
      "type": "table",
      "columns": [
        "Policy",
        "Behavior"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "`None` or not set",
          "No dirty-state enforcement"
        ],
        [
          "`allow_dirty`",
          "Passes regardless of dirty files"
        ],
        [
          "`clean`",
          "Blocks/fails if any dirty files exist (dirty_count > 0 or conflicted_count > 0)"
        ],
        [
          "`allow_listed_dirty`",
          "Allows dirty paths listed in `ValidateArgs.paths`; blocks if unlisted dirty paths exist"
        ]
      ],
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-47",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Dirty-policy enforcement runs after path normalization. `ValidateArgs.paths` are normalized via `_normalize_validate_paths()` before being compared against `before_git_state.dirty_paths` (workspace-relative POSIX paths from git porcelain parsing). This means relative, absolute, and `./`-prefixed paths are all resolved to their canonical workspace-relative form before the `allow_listed_dirty` comparison.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-48",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "`_check_dirty_policy()` from `validate_git.py` is the single policy authority. `Validate.run()` no longer inlines dirty-policy logic that compares raw `args.paths` against dirty paths.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-49",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "When `expected_dirty_policy` is set and the policy fails, the validation yields a `ValidateResult` with `status=\"failed\"`, `error_kind=\"dirty_workspace\"`, and a `blocker_summary` containing `dirty_workspace: 1`.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-50",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "worktree-readiness Profile",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-51",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "A new profile with no lint/test/schema commands. Purely git state collection and dirty policy enforcement. Suitable for answering \"is this lane clean enough for handoff or aggregation?\"",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-52",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Checks: none (git state is collected by the run() method, not profile checks)",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-53",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Receipt Content-Light Behavior",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-54",
